A||N||1||KRMFiero||Ford (JBL) Factory amp question||||1||
Z||000000||KRMFiero||12-16-2001||09:58 PM||||Alright, I just took the factory amp system out of my '90 Ford SHO    I am going to install it in my fiero  but what wires are what?    the silver amp has two power wires comming out - Yellow (Very thick) and a Semi Thick red one. It looked as if the red one was grounded to the chassie but it probley wasnt. then that amp has 3 wires going to the black JBL amp (i usume input wires) then 2 more wires going out to sub.<P>the black JBL amp has 3 wires going to gray amp. and 2 wiring harness. one a very thing guage and 1 a thick gauge<P>thin guage:<BR>bare silver wire<BR>green<BR>white /w orange<BR>lt blue<BR>lt blue /w black<BR>brown<BR>yellow<BR>white /w green<BR>purple /w white<P>those are the thin wires and apear to be inputs?  F0DF-14588-DB on harness<P>thicker guage harness:<BR>lt blue /w white<BR>brown /w white<BR>green /w orange<BR>pink / blue<BR>pink /w green<BR>orange /w green<BR>blue /w pink<BR>white /w green<BR>dr blue<P>F0DB-EE-19B113 on harness, these aprea to be outputs, what is that? <P><BR>help me out<BR>Thanks<BR>Kyle<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||MoneypitGT||12-16-2001||11:47 PM||||Yellow is constant power, your red is ground. Jbl amp, one wire is turn on, the other two are your inputs, some are RCA level some are speaker. Gray amp was for the interior speakers, those colors sound like standard Ford speaker wire colors, which are usually twisted in speaker pairs. The one plug is input and the other is output, you will have to figure that out. But one question, why in the hell do you want to go through the hassle to put that in the Fiero? The thing that made the JBL setup sound good was the speakers, the amps aren't really that much power. Hope this helps a little bit.<BR> Chris<P>------------------<BR>  <B>Check out my site at:</B>   <A HREF="http://www.customdynamix.com" TARGET=_blank>www.customdynamix.com</A> <BR>Turbo Q4 GT Project||||reg||10
